  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 6.875,
      "text": "An entity-relationship diagram is a map of tables before they become SQL, or beside the SQL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 6.875,
      "end": 8.611,
      "text": "A box is an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 8.611,
      "end": 11.555,
      "text": "The name on the box is the table you expect.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 11.555,
      "end": 14.18,
      "text": "Inside the box you list attributes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 14.18,
      "end": 15.972,
      "text": "You mark the primary key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 15.972,
      "end": 20.236,
      "text": "You mark foreign keys as copies of someone else's primary key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 20.236,
      "end": 22.375,
      "text": "A line is a relationship.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 22.375,
      "end": 26.722,
      "text": "The ends of the line carry cardinality: one or many.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 26.722,
      "end": 28.569,
      "text": "A crow's foot means many.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 28.569,
      "end": 30.375,
      "text": "A single bar means one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 30.375,
      "end": 32.875,
      "text": "A circle means zero is allowed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 32.875,
      "end": 35.444,
      "text": "A second bar means one is required.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 35.444,
      "end": 38.347,
      "text": "You do not need every symbol on day one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 38.347,
      "end": 41.902,
      "text": "You need boxes, keys, and honest lines.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 41.902,
      "end": 43.916,
      "text": "Read a line as a sentence.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 43.916,
      "end": 46.319,
      "text": "One customer places many orders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 46.319,
      "end": 48.875,
      "text": "Each order belongs to one customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 48.875,
      "end": 52.638,
      "text": "If you cannot say the sentence, the line is decoration.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 52.638,
      "end": 55.847,
      "text": "Do not draw a line labeled after a one-off demo.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 55.847,
      "end": 58.027,
      "text": "Draw the store you are actually building.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 58.027,
      "end": 62.805,
      "text": "Keep example names ordinary: customers, orders, books.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 62.805,
      "end": 67.555,
      "text": "A diagram that uses joke names will be quoted as if they were tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 67.555,
      "end": 71.458,
      "text": "Attributes that are only display labels stay off the line.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 71.458,
      "end": 73.666,
      "text": "The line is not where you write total.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 73.666,
      "end": 75.486,
      "text": "total lives in a box.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 75.486,
      "end": 79.597,
      "text": "When a relationship has its own attributes, it wants a box.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 79.597,
      "end": 81.277,
      "text": "Enrollment has a grade.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 81.277,
      "end": 83.5,
      "text": "That is the many-to-many lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 83.5,
      "end": 87.291,
      "text": "On the diagram, the middle box is a real entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 87.291,
      "end": 88.986,
      "text": "Layout is pedagogy.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 88.986,
      "end": 90.93,
      "text": "Put the hub table in the middle.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 90.93,
      "end": 94.236,
      "text": "customers in the center, orders to the side.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 94.236,
      "end": 96.597,
      "text": "Do not cross lines if you can avoid it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 96.597,
      "end": 99.277,
      "text": "The drawing should match the join you will write.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 99.277,
      "end": 101.847,
      "text": "Update the diagram when you ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 101.847,
      "end": 104.111,
      "text": "A stale picture is worse than none.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 104.111,
      "end": 107.194,
      "text": "The point is not software that draws cylinders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 107.194,
      "end": 114.319,
      "text": "The point is a shared sentence: these are the things, these are the keys, these are the allowed counts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.319,
      "end": 117.083,
      "text": "Crow's foot is not the only notation.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 117.083,
      "end": 120.486,
      "text": "Chen diagrams use diamonds for relationships.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 120.486,
      "end": 126.152,
      "text": "IDEF1X uses dots and crow's feet with different mandatory marks.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 126.152,
      "end": 128.25,
      "text": "Pick one notation for a team.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 128.25,
      "end": 132.861,
      "text": "Mixing them is how a bar gets read as optional when it meant mandatory.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 132.861,
      "end": 138.416,
      "text": "Subtype boxes appear when a customer is either a person or an organization.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 138.416,
      "end": 140.583,
      "text": "That is a later modeling choice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 140.583,
      "end": 144.472,
      "text": "Do not draw it on day one unless the facts already split.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 144.472,
      "end": 146.208,
      "text": "Color is not notation.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 146.208,
      "end": 150.819,
      "text": "A calm diagram in one ink beats a rainbow of departments.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 150.819,
      "end": 154.319,
      "text": "Your player uses a dark calm stage for the same reason.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 154.319,
      "end": 158.805,
      "text": "Print the diagram at the size a new engineer can read on one screen.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 158.805,
      "end": 162.722,
      "text": "If you need a poster, you have too many boxes for one talk.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 162.722,
      "end": 167.722,
      "text": "Split by bounded context: catalog, checkout, fulfillment.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 167.722,
      "end": 171.541,
      "text": "Each picture should still use the same names for the shared keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 171.541,
      "end": 175.819,
      "text": "customer_id is customer_id everywhere.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 175.819,
      "end": 179.652,
      "text": "A glossary next to the pictures beats clever synonyms.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 179.652,
      "end": 184.819,
      "text": "When a line has numbers, 1 and 0..* are enough.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 184.819,
      "end": 187.069,
      "text": "Do not write a paragraph on the line.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 187.069,
      "end": 190.375,
      "text": "Put the paragraph in a comment on the foreign key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 190.375,
      "end": 192.263,
      "text": "The diagram is the map.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 192.263,
      "end": 194.277,
      "text": "The SQL is the territory.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 194.277,
      "end": 197.625,
      "text": "Walk both, in that order, until they agree.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 197.625,
      "end": 200.666,
      "text": "Then the next join is a line you already drew.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 200.666,
      "end": 204.736,
      "text": "A diagram that cannot be read in two minutes is a mural.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 204.736,
      "end": 206.347,
      "text": "Murals do not ship.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 206.347,
      "end": 210.111,
      "text": "Cut until a new person can say the sentences on the lines.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 210.111,
      "end": 215.083,
      "text": "If they invent a table that is not on the page, the page is incomplete.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 215.083,
      "end": 219.527,
      "text": "If they cannot find a table that is in SQL, the page is stale.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 219.527,
      "end": 224.541,
      "text": "Incomplete and stale are the only two diagram failures that matter.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 224.541,
      "end": 225.916,
      "text": "Pretty is optional.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 225.916,
      "end": 227.319,
      "text": "Agreement is not.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 227.319,
      "end": 228.569,
      "text": "Print the keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 228.569,
      "end": 229.875,
      "text": "Print the counts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 229.875,
      "end": 231.666,
      "text": "Sit the SQL beside it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 231.666,
      "end": 233.916,
      "text": "When they match, you have a map.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 233.916,
      "end": 242.861,
      "text": "An entity-relationship diagram is a picture of what you will store and how those things connect, drawn before CREATE TABLE hardens a guess.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 242.861,
      "end": 246.763,
      "text": "Entities are the things: customer, product, order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 246.763,
      "end": 248.68,
      "text": "They appear as rectangles.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 248.68,
      "end": 255.861,
      "text": "Attributes are the facts inside the rectangle: name, email, price, with types once you know them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 255.861,
      "end": 263.263,
      "text": "Relationships are how entities participate: a customer places an order, an order contains products.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 263.263,
      "end": 271.944,
      "text": "Chen notation uses diamonds for relationships, and it showed up in a 1976 paper, which is why textbooks still teach it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 271.944,
      "end": 281.166,
      "text": "Crow's foot notation uses lines and little marks at the ends for cardinality, and practitioners sketch it on whiteboards because it is fast.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 281.166,
      "end": 282.625,
      "text": "Neither is more true.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 282.625,
      "end": 285.5,
      "text": "Switching mid-diagram is what is false.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 285.626,
      "end": 294.645,
      "text": "A complete diagram names the entities, the attributes you will actually store, the relationships, and the cardinalities once you know them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 294.645,
      "end": 297.978,
      "text": "It is a map, not a screenshot of the application.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 297.978,
      "end": 299.603,
      "text": "Screens have buttons.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 299.603,
      "end": 302.506,
      "text": "Diagrams have identity and connection.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 302.506,
      "end": 305.589,
      "text": "Start by placing the entities you already found.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 305.589,
      "end": 311.423,
      "text": "Then ask, for each pair that your interviews connected, whether a relationship belongs.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 311.423,
      "end": 313.353,
      "text": "Not every pair gets a line.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 313.353,
      "end": 317.784,
      "text": "Customers and manufacturers might only meet through products.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 317.784,
      "end": 319.298,
      "text": "Draw the real verb.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 319.298,
      "end": 323.228,
      "text": "places, contains, reviews, works for.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 323.228,
      "end": 327.117,
      "text": "If you cannot name the verb, you do not have a relationship yet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 327.117,
      "end": 329.381,
      "text": "You have two boxes on a poster.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 329.381,
      "end": 332.52,
      "text": "Cardinality marks wait for the next lessons.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 332.52,
      "end": 338.826,
      "text": "Here the skill is connecting without spaghetti: every line is a sentence from requirements.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 338.826,
      "end": 341.034,
      "text": "The benefit is forgetting less.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 341.034,
      "end": 345.492,
      "text": "A missing line is a join you will fake with a comment in six months.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 345.492,
      "end": 349.076,
      "text": "An extra line is a constraint you cannot explain.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 349.076,
      "end": 352.117,
      "text": "Read the diagram out loud as sentences.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 352.117,
      "end": 356.02,
      "text": "If a sentence was never said in gathering, erase the line.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 356.02,
      "end": 359.742,
      "text": "If a sentence was said and there is no line, draw it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 359.742,
      "end": 364.923,
      "text": "Then you are ready to talk about one, many, and identifying relationships.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
